    "body": "STOPPED at Step 5. Claim released.\n\nUpstream main 31f8d03d744e77ce707282d816e11efe0922f239 has no ChatBackend trait or AI chat panel. The search `rg -n 'ChatBackend|Tab::AiChat|session/cancel' crates` returns no matches. Issue #1946 is still open, and there is no open panel PR to stack on.\n\nInbox::listen(port, wake), listen_with_idle(port, wake, idle), and bridge(addr, input, output) have no authentication configuration. A pin cannot enable token authentication through those APIs. Treating ordinary unauthenticated mode as tokenized would test the wrong contract.\n\nI could not write a runnable behavioral pin for the required fake ACP multi-step turn through the panel backend trait. Missing-symbol compilation errors would not prove that behavior. Implementing the missing panel would also implement separate issue #1946.\n\nNo production files or tests changed. No builds, mutations, or gates ran. Resume #1948 after #1946 supplies the panel/backend seam.\n\nFile overlaps only: #1738 adds unrelated MCP module declarations; #2029, #1938, and #1798 add unrelated UI module declarations. None changes the listener or bridge functions.\n",
